{"r":45,"c":[[71,"Resetting the sensor is possible by cycling VDD level or by writing a soft reset command. Cycling the"]]}
{"r":46,"c":[[71,"VDDIO level will not cause a reset."]]}
{"r":47,"c":[[71,"3.3"],[99,"Sensor modes"]]}
{"r":48,"c":[[71,"The BME280 offers three sensor modes: sleep mode, forced mode and normal mode. These can be"]]}
{"r":49,"c":[[71,"selected using the mode[1:0] setting (see chapter 5.4.5). The available modes are:"]]}
{"r":50,"c":[[89,"•"],[107,"Sleep mode: no operation, all registers accessible, lowest power, selected after startup"]]}
{"r":51,"c":[[89,"•"],[107,"Forced mode: perform one measurement, store results and return to sleep mode"]]}
{"r":52,"c":[[89,"•"],[107,"Normal mode: perpetual cycling of measurements and inactive periods."]]}
